Also amended the `beforeRender()` docblock, which claimed the hook runs "on every frame, even when the render cache is valid". Nothing in the component overrides it, so the audience is userland, and reusing a cached subtree means descendants are not visited at all. That was already true on base when an ancestor cache hit; this makes it the common case, so the wording had to go. `ScheduledTickTrait` (LoaderWidget, ProgressBarWidget) stays the mechanism for work that must run every frame.

Left `shiftSubtree()` without a visited set on purpose: `AbstractWidget` has a single `$parent` pointer and `PositionTracker` keys a `WeakMap` by instance, so a widget added twice can only hold one rect anyway, and on base the second `setWidgetRect()` already won. Guarding here would only make this one recursion consistent about a topology that invalidation does not support either, at the cost of an allocation on the per-frame path. `ContainerWidget::add()` would be the place if you want to reject it.
